.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt SND_CS35L54 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm snd_cs35l54
.Nd "Cirrus Logic CS35L54 speaker amplifier driver"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
The driver is loaded at boot by
.Xr devmatch 8
when the amplifiers are present.
To load it explicitly, place the following line in
.Xr rc.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kld_list="snd_cs35l54"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Some laptops route the internal speakers through smart amplifiers that sit
on an I2C bus, behind the HDA codec driven by
.Xr snd_hda 4 .
These amplifiers stay silent until their DSP firmware is downloaded and
they are told to play.
.Pp
The
.Nm
driver attaches to the ACPI device that describes the amplifiers and reads
the amplifier addresses, the platform subsystem id, and the shared reset
line from it.
It downloads the DSP program and one tuning file per amplifier, applies the
factory speaker calibration stored in the UEFI variable
.Va CirrusSmartAmpCalibrationData ,
and starts or pauses the amplifiers whenever
.Xr snd_hda 4
starts or stops a stream to the internal speakers.
.Pp
The firmware download needs the root file system: when the driver attaches
before it is mounted, the download waits for it.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports Cirrus Logic CS35L54 amplifiers, revision B0, attached by
I2C and described by the ACPI hardware id
.Li CSC3554 ,
including:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
HP ZBook Ultra G1a 14 inch Mobile Workstation
.El
.Sh FILES
The firmware files come from linux-firmware and are named after the ACPI
subsystem id
.Ar sub
in lower case, with
.Ar N
the amplifier index starting at 1:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /boot/firmware/cirrus/cs35l54-b0-dsp1-misc- Ns Ar sub Ns Pa .wmfw
DSP program.
.It Pa /boot/firmware/cirrus/cs35l54-b0-dsp1-misc- Ns Ar sub Ns Pa -amp Ns Ar N Ns Pa .bin
Tuning of amplifier
.Ar N .
.El
.Pp
The driver first asks
.Xr firmware 9
for a firmware module image of the same name with
.Ql / ,
.Ql -
and
.Ql \&.
replaced by
.Ql _ ,
then for the raw file.
The
.Pa audio/sound-firmware-cirrus-kmod
port installs the raw files;
.Xr fwget 8
detects the amplifiers and installs it.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va dev.cs35l54.%d.loaded
Read-only, 1 once the firmware is downloaded.
.It Va dev.cs35l54.%d.play
1 while the amplifiers play.
Writing 1 or 0 starts or pauses them by hand, for tests.
.It Va dev.cs35l54.%d.volume
Amplifier volume in dB, from -100 to 12.
The default is -30.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gpio 4 ,
.Xr snd_hda 4 ,
.Xr sound 4 ,
.Xr devmatch 8 ,
.Xr fwget 8 ,
.Xr firmware 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
The
.Nm
driver and this manual page were written by
.An Olivier Cochard-Labbe Aq Mt olivier@FreeBSD.org .
.Sh CAVEATS
The reset line is a GPIO of the AMD GPIO controller.
If the
.Cm amdgpio
module is not loaded before the driver attaches, the driver only wakes
the amplifiers and cannot reset them; add it to
.Va kld_list
to use the reset line.
.Pp
The amplifier interrupt is not used.
.Sh BUGS
Through
.Xr ig4 4 ,
the first 32-bit word of each read from the amplifiers is stale; the driver
reads one extra word and drops it.
.Pp
Only the HP ZBook Ultra G1a has been tested.
CS35L56 and CS35L57 amplifiers, speaker-id variants, and SPI or SoundWire
attachment are not supported.
